String : A String is a collection of character which is defined in java.lang pacakages and it is immutable in nature.
         it provides various number of methods used to manipulate data in String.
         
String is most commonly used data type in java thats why it is immutable in nature i. means once the String object crteated 
its value cannot be changed which promotes : Security, Better memory optimization, String pool optimization.

What is String Pool in java?
- String pool is a special memory area in java heap memory which store the unique copy of String literal and allow JVm 
 to reuse that literal to Save extra memory.
 
What is Null Pointer Exception :
A Null Pointer Exception in java is runtime exception which occur when our program tries to access the object reference 
which has no object or maybe a null pointed to it.exception

